1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,720
Scout's Eye. Explainable U19 match intelligence, built on Microsoft Foundry.

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:19,800
A U19 title decider. Northbridge need a draw, Vallora need a win. Second minute:
goal. A fact card appears instantly, then the agents' verified commentary replaces it.

3
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:32,070
Same moment, two audiences. Fans get the story. Analysts get field tilt,
PPDA and momentum, from the same verified facts, in English or Hungarian.

4
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:45,260
Click any overlay to see why it exists: the source events, the data, and the
rule behind every claim. If the text says dominating, the numbers have to prove it.

5
00:00:50,200 --> 00:01:07,400
Five agents work together in a Microsoft Agent Framework workflow. The Match Analyst
decides what matters, Narrators write each version, and a Verifier checks every number,
name and claim. Here the pre-check caught an unsupported claim and sent the text back for one repair.

6
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:21,510
Player focus: a fifteen-year-old full-back, still on the
bench at thirty minutes, and the note says so. Low data, so
no ranking claim. The model never knew who the planted talents were.

7
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:35,660
Forty-ninth minute: a Vallora penalty wins the title. The fact card comes first, then the
verified text. The recap tells the story, and its numbers are checked against the match facts.

8
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:51,200
Synthetic data, checked against published U19 benchmarks. Five agents, one rule:
never show a number you cannot prove. Scout's Eye. Try the live demo, link below.

